From a711523f0d7942357fab6deae4bd38d93b2e4e29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Mar 2026 18:11:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 262/913] dts: stm32: use correct SPI for parent of EXTI 19 for
 stm32mp15

EXTI node for stm32mp15 in OP-TEE must use the RTC_WKUP_ALARM_S (SPI 198),
i.e. RTC wakeup timer and alarms (A and B) secure interrupt as source of
EXTI 19 = RTC wakeup timer and alarm (A and B) wakeup
(ORed non-secure: RTC_WKUP_ALARM_S, SPI 3
 and      secure: RTC_WKUP_ALARM_S, SPI 198).

Linux use the non secure interrupt but OP-TEE must use the secure
interruption so we have a difference in STM32MP15 Soc device tree
between secure and non secure world on this interrupt line.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 54d3afdfac6f921d71b4c2a2e97cf308094a748e dts: stm32: use correct SPI for parent of EXTI 19 for stm32mp15]
Signed-off-by: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Ia15a668a98e3952d2b2826a3d4c32208cae4690b
---
 core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp151.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp151.dtsi b/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp151.dtsi
index a4b0b99a5..9dc8c52fd 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp151.dtsi
+++ b/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp151.dtsi
@@ -198,7 +198,7 @@
 				<&intc GIC_SPI 1   IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 				<0>,
 				<0>,
-				<&intc GIC_SPI 3   IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				<&intc GIC_SPI 198 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 				<0>,						/* EXTI_20 */
 				<&intc GIC_SPI 31  IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 				<&intc GIC_SPI 33  IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-- 
2.53.0

